  "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $P:$ $2>6$\n\n- $Q:$ $10$ is an integer number.\n\n- $R:$ $7$ is a composite number.",
  "worked_solution": "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate the truth value of each statement:\n\n- Statement $P$ is *false* because $2≯6.$\n\n- Statement $Q$ is *true.* Indeed, $10$ is an integer number.\n\n- Statement $R$ is *false* because $7$ is not a composite number (it is a prime number).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Q$ only.\"",
